{% call s.prose({ width: "narrow" }) %}
  <p>Is an intensive right for everyone? Honestly, no. If either of you is in acute crisis, or safety is a concern, a different level of care comes first, and we'll help you find it. An intensive works best when both people are willing to spend a day looking honestly at the relationship as something you're both part of, not a courtroom where one of you is on trial.</p>
  <p>Intensives are scheduled directly with Kay, and the length (anywhere from four to eight hours) depends on what you're working on. Ongoing weekly couples and marriage therapy is available too, and the intensive can sit alongside it or stand on its own. The simplest first step is the free call, where we sort out which shape fits.</p>
